PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID="project-id"
PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET="dataset"
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:4321

SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID="project-id"
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET="dataset"

### Contact form
# Formspree endpoint the contact form POSTs to (https://formspree.io/f/<form-id>).
# The site is statically built, so this value is baked into the HTML at build
# time and is therefore public by design.
FORMSPREE_URL="https://formspree.io/f/your-form-id"

### Deployment
# The site is prerendered and deployed as an assets-only Cloudflare Worker
# (see wrangler.jsonc). Every variable above is read at *build* time — nothing is
# bound to the Worker at request time — so they belong in the Workers Builds
# "Build variables" settings (Settings -> Build), or in this file locally.
# Setting them as Worker variables/secrets does nothing: the build never sees them.
#
# Local check: npm run cf:preview    Deploy: npm run cf:deploy
